  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Crowd 1st Set Intro & Tuning**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 6 archived performances [8]\n- **Women Are Smarter**: rare: 9 archived performances [8]\n- **How Sweet It Is (To Be Loved By You)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [8]\n- **Crowd 2nd Set Intro & Tuning**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [8]\n- **Lazy River Road**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [8]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2024-08-01.Nak700** (recommended): source not stated; 24 songs; 218 min [1]\n- **deadco2024-08-01**: source not stated; 21 songs; 223 min; rated 4/5 by 1 [3]\n- **deadco2024-08-01.GD**: audience recording; 21 songs; 220 min; rated 1.67/5 by 3 [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Billed as the Dead Forever finale at the Sphere, with Weir, Hart, Mayer and Burbridge on stage [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2024-08-01.Nak700**: taped by Biran Dyke; transferred by Eric Lugassy; source: Nakamichi CM-700 Cardioids > EAA PSP2 @ 55db > Sound Devices 702T [1]. Also: Captured with Nakamichi CM-700 cardioid mics through an EAA PSP2 preamp into a Sound Devices 702T, then edited in Reaper and saved as 24-bit FLAC; Taper recorded from section 102 behind row 37, roughly eight feet up, using a NOS mic arrangement [1]\n- **deadco2024-08-01**: taped by DREXELATLHEEL; transferred by Cam Keough; source: Sony PCM A10 (internal mics) 16/48 [3]. Also: Recorded with a Sony PCM A10 using internal mics at 16-bit/48k, processed through Adobe Audition and CD Wave, then THL; Patched with a second source from DREXELATLHEEL, recorded with SP-CMC-8u mics into an SPSB10 and a Sony A10; Reviewer asks whether the Sony PCM A10 16/48 internal-mic recording was merely upconverted to 24-bit FLAC [3][4]\n- **deadco2024-08-01.GD**: taped by Tony Jenkins; transferred by TJ; source: Audience MAster [2]",
